.TH MAIL 1 "2026-08-17" "mail 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mail \- read and search Apple Mail from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mail
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mail
is a read\-only command\-line tool for searching and analyzing Apple Mail.
It reads Mail's Envelope Index and .emlx files directly and emits JSONL by
default, so output streams and pipes cleanly into scripts and LLM agents.
.PP
Nothing under
.I ~/Library/Mail
is ever written or modified. The only command that writes files is
.BR export ,
and it refuses to write inside Mail's own data directory.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
macOS with Apple Mail configured, and
.B Full Disk Access
granted to the terminal application (not the
.B mail
binary). System Settings \(-> Privacy & Security \(-> Full Disk Access.
The
.B trash
command additionally requires
.B Automation
permission for the terminal to control Mail.
.PP
Run
.B "mail doctor"
first to verify access.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
success, including zero results
.TP
.B 1
general error
.TP
.B 2
Full Disk Access missing
.TP
.B 3
Automation permission missing (trash only)
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B "mail doctor [--check-automation]"
Verify access to Mail's data and report what it found.
.TP
.B "mail search [query]"
Search messages. Metadata filters are instant; a bare
.I query
searches message bodies.
.TP
.B "mail show <id>"
Show one message in full, by ROWID.
.TP
.B "mail links"
Extract normalized URLs from matching messages.
.TP
.B "mail export --out <dir> [--as eml|json|mbox]"
Write matching messages to a directory you name.
.TP
.B "mail stats"
Emit one aggregate summary record over the matching messages.
.TP
.B "mail trash [id]"
Move messages to Trash (recoverable, never permanent).
.TP
.B "mail reference"
Print the full reference guide embedded in the binary.
.SH SHARED FILTERS
Every message\-selecting command accepts the same flags:
.BR \-\-from ,
.BR \-\-to ,
.BR \-\-subject ,
.BR \-\-mailbox ,
.BR \-\-since ,
.BR \-\-until ,
.BR \-\-unread ,
.BR \-\-flagged ,
.BR \-\-has\-attachment ,
and
.BR \-\-limit .
.PP
.B \-\-limit
defaults to 50 for
.BR search ,
and to 0 (unlimited) for
.BR links ,
.BR export ,
.BR stats ,
and
.BR trash .
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
.BR \-\-format " jsonl" " (default), " json ", " table ", or " text .
JSONL is the contract: one JSON object per line, streamed as results are
parsed. Errors go to stderr, so stdout stays pipeable.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mail search \-\-from linkedin \-\-since 30d
mail search "invoice" \-\-since 90d
mail show 48213
mail links \-\-from linkedin | jq \-r '.url_canonical'
mail export \-\-out ./archive \-\-since 1y \-\-as mbox
mail stats \-\-since 6m
mail trash \-\-from linkedin \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
Run
.B "mail reference"
for the complete guide: output schema, gotchas, and recipes.
